From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:16:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/54] wayland: give toplevels that ask for it a server-side
 title bar

Implement zxdg_decoration_manager_v1. A toplevel whose client asks for
server-side decorations, or leaves the choice to the compositor, gets a
40 pixel title bar at the top of its frame rect, outside the client's
window geometry; clients that ask for client-side decorations or never
bind the protocol keep drawing their own, so no window gets two.

The title bar height travels with each configuration and applies when
the client acks it: configures send the frame size minus the title bar,
the acked geometry grows by it, the buffer rect covers it with the
surfaces moved below it, and min and max sizes, popup positions and
window menu points account for it. Fullscreen windows have none.

MetaWindow:titlebar-height tells the shell how tall a title bar to draw,
and meta_window_has_rounded_corners() whether to round it like the
window, so it can draw the bar, its controls and the window shadow as
children of the window actor.

Upstream-Status: luft-only GNOME doesn't draw server-side decorations for Wayland clients; Kestrel's shell draws the bar
